{"uid":"929c12d0780409a","name":"test_a_target_is_recorded_once_when_delivery_and_shutdown_race","fullName":"tests.test_events_webhooks#test_a_target_is_recorded_once_when_delivery_and_shutdown_race","historyId":"2485ae78ef4db5110098f96b89cc8c4a","time":{"start":1791912158131,"stop":1791912158674,"duration":543},"description":"One event, one target, one row — even when both writers reach it.\n\n    Cancelling ``asyncio.to_thread`` does **not** stop the worker thread: the ``await``\n    raises immediately while the POST keeps running to completion. So at shutdown two\n    writers can settle the same target — the delivery thread finishing\n    ``_deliver_with_retry``, and ``stop()``'s drain walking ``_in_flight`` — and the event\n    was dead-lettered twice, once ``exhausted`` and once ``shutdown``. An operator saw two\n    rows for one delivery and would double-count it on replay.\n\n    This surfaced as an intermittent failure in an unrelated assertion\n    (``letters[\"count\"] == 1`` seeing ``2``) and moved between tests run to run, which is\n    what a race looks like from the outside. Reproduced deterministically here by holding\n    the sender inside the POST, stopping while it is held, and only then releasing it — so\n    the drain runs first and the thread finishes second, which is the losing order.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>One event, one target, one row — even when both writers reach it.</p>\n<pre><code>Cancelling ``asyncio.to_thread`` does **not** stop the worker thread: the ``await``\nraises immediately while the POST keeps running to completion. So at shutdown two\nwriters can settle the same target — the delivery thread finishing\n``_deliver_with_retry``, and ``stop()``'s drain walking ``_in_flight`` — and the event\nwas dead-lettered twice, once ``exhausted`` and once ``shutdown``. An operator saw two\nrows for one delivery and would double-count it on replay.\n\nThis surfaced as an intermittent failure in an unrelated assertion\n(``letters[&quot;count&quot;] == 1`` seeing ``2``) and moved between tests run to run, which is\nwhat a race looks like from the outside. Reproduced deterministically here by holding\nthe sender inside the POST, stopping while it is held, and only then releasing it — so\nthe drain runs first and the thread finishes second, which is the losing order.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791911682419,"stop":1791911682419,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_asyncio_loop_factory","time":{"start":1791911683283,"stop":1791911683283,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791911687464,"stop":1791911687465,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_default_tests_to_trusted_header_auth","time":{"start":1791912157574,"stop":1791912157575,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_clear_prompt_info_cache","time":{"start":1791912157574,"stop":1791912157574,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791912157574,"stop":1791912157574,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldD